-- title:
--   Original full negative-jump Laplace functional from all Borel Poisson count laws and finite-family spatial independence
-- statement:
--   A finite-activity original spectrally negative Lévy source has the exact full causal negative-jump Laplace expectation if its original marked counting measure is known to have the Poisson marginal law on every negative Borel set and joint independence on every finite family of spatially disjoint negative Borel mark sets. This isolates the Poisson random-measure Laplace-functional/monotone approximation theorem from the stochastic independence of physical marks. Marginal Poisson count laws alone do not suffice; joint spatial independence is an essential separate hypothesis.
-- source:
--   Rigorous reduction of original a77 f4b58008 to Proved negative Borel Poisson marginals and a new original source independent count frontier, preserving actual probability measure/finite activity and physical jump sum.

import Mathlib
